course: dictionary
lesson: 4091
title: Gigantic: extremely big
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words around a new word, and they often give clues to its meaning. «The gigantic castle towered over the village.» Towered over tells you the castle was very tall, so gigantic must mean extremely big.
explain: A good check is to swap in a word that fits, such as huge or enormous, and see if the sentence still makes sense. «A gigantic wave» works with huge or enormous, so you know the meaning is close.
explain: Gigantic comes from giant, so it means big like a giant. Writers choose it when they want to make something sound impressive, but one strong describing word works better than a pile of them.
fact: Gigantic is an adjective, a describing word, and it means extremely big, like a giant.
fact: «Gigantic» often describes monsters, castles, waves, and stars in stories and science.
fact: Phrases such as «a gigantic wave» and «gigantic footprints» show a huge size.
fact: The Sun is a star: a gigantic ball of very hot gas that makes its own light and heat.
fact: Piling up «big, enormous, gigantic» says big three times, so choose one or two sharp adjectives instead.
exercise: «The gigantic castle towered over the village.» What does gigantic mean? | Far away | Old and broken | Very small | *Extremely big
exercise: Which word could replace gigantic in «a gigantic wave»? | Soft | Tiny | *Enormous | Quiet
exercise: Ella says «the big, enormous, gigantic dog» is great writing. What is the better advice? | Never use describing words | Use the word big three times | *Use two sharp adjectives that each add something new | Use as many describing words as you can
test: «The Sun is a gigantic ball of very hot gas.» What is gigantic describing? | Something quiet | Something cold | Something made of wood | *Something extremely big
test: Which phrase shows a gigantic size? | *a gigantic footprint | a short pencil | a tiny pebble | a small whisper
exam: Which sentence uses gigantic correctly? | The gigantic whisper was barely heard | *The gigantic cake filled the whole table | The gigantic pebble fitted in my pocket
